    "section_summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "extract_value": "This section describes the Eating Disorder Examination Questionnaire (EDE-Q) as a 36-item self-report measure with four subscales (restraint, eating concern, shape concern, weight concern) and notes that a global score can be obtained by averaging the subscales. It reports that the Portuguese and original versions have good psychometric properties (\u03b1=0.94) and that in the present study the global and subscale EDE-Q scores had Cronbach's alpha values ranging from 0.77 to 0.95. The section does not provide study-level sample, demographic, BMI, assessment of body appreciation, survey method, or number of studies information.",
      "evidence_source": "The EDE-Q is a 36-item self-report measure that evaluates the frequency and intensity of eating pathology-related attitudes and behaviours. ... In the present study, the global and subscale's score of EDE-Q presented a Cronbach's alpha ranging from 0.77 to 0.95.",
